  "title": "Neural interactions in the human frontal cortex dissociate reward and punishment learning (Combrisson et al., 2024): preprocessed SEEG high-gamma power, 16 patients (derivative)",
  "description": "Preprocessed stereotactic EEG (SEEG) high-gamma power (50-100 Hz) from 16 patients with pharmaco-resistant epilepsy performing a probabilistic instrumental learning task with reward and punishment conditions. The derivative dataset contains bipolar derivations in anterior insula, dorsolateral prefrontal, lateral orbitofrontal and ventromedial prefrontal cortex, time-locked to the outcome. It supports information-theoretic analyses of how distinct frontal subsystems encode reward and punishment prediction errors.",
  "methods_description": "Patients with depth electrodes (Dixi) performed a probabilistic instrumental learning task with reward and punishment pairs of abstract cues. Original iEEG was recorded at 512 or 1024 Hz. Bipolar derivations in grey matter were computed, and gamma power (50-100 Hz) was estimated with a multitaper transform, down-sampled to 256 Hz and time-locked to the outcome. Trial-wise prediction errors came from a Q-learning model.",
